# Build output. Everything the compiler and the shade plugin produce.
target/

# VVCS's own repository data, wherever one has been created.
#
# This project *is* a version control system, so its storage directories are working data
# rather than source. They are also content-addressed and machine-local: a .vvcs directory
# copied between machines carries absolute paths from the machine that made it.
.vvcs/

# The sample project's media.
#
# 201MB of .mp4 that the code never reads. The parser takes the file path from the
# "resource" property in the .kdenlive XML as a string and records it as an asset; it never
# opens the media itself, so parsing, the diff engine, the API and the viewer all work
# without these files. They are also third-party footage whose redistribution is not ours to
# grant, and at 99MB the largest is close enough to GitHub's 100MB per-file limit to be a
# bad bet. sample.kdenlive is kept, so the tests and the demo still run.
#
# To get the media back for local Kdenlive work, fetch it separately rather than committing
# it.
sample-project/*.mp4
sample-project/*.mov
sample-project/*.wav

# Eclipse. These are per-developer, and .classpath in particular names absolute paths.
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.factorypath

# Node, should the frontend ever grow a build step. The frontend is plain ES modules today
# and needs none of this; it is here so that a later change does not commit 200MB of it.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
out/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor scratch files
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.*.orig
.*.rej

# Logs
*.log
